Z||000016||Haze_Performance||05-10-2001||12:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B>i saw that northstar and archies finale race and the northstar killed that finale-i would of hated to be archie then!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I didn't see the race.. I was riding along during a test drive (87 GT)<P>But don't forget... Archie was beating the snot out of the Finale. (He was giving many many 100+mph test drives before the race) + Its having valve problems. The North* is a very nice conversion, but I think I would still stick with the SBC over it.<P><B>Ride on Arch!!! You da man!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">      </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
Z||000017||KissMySSFiero||05-10-2001||12:24 AM||||I was in the car when they raced.   he didnt get beat that bad.  only off the line then he kept up.  had a late shift into second.  not to mention the guy with the N* has about all the power he can get(not many performance parts for that motor)  and and archie had a taxi cab replacement eng in the finale.  for the price that guy could have had a tpi 350 and a finale kit.  but then again he wouldnt have the N*<BR>and i got to see it all from the passenger seat.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000018||SloPonti||05-11-2001||12:51 AM||||well i hate to say it but i rode in archies car to and i was not all that inpressed! he told me that motor was at 270hp and the northstar is 290! archie got a head start on the nortstart-the northstar guy wanted to do a dead stop race and archie did a rolling start - we all watched as the nortstar pulled about 3 car lengths ahead of the finale! now i am not sure of the weight of the finale because it is a body kit as apposed to the northstar! also the motor in archies car is not a taxi cab motor-it is a tpi motor out of a camaro or firebird! i know you can put alot of upgrades to archies motor to get more hp-i would like to take a ride in pauls v8 and see how fast a more hp fiero is! but riding in archies finale was alot like riding in my 87 iroc 305 auto! it just did not feel extremely fast to me! just my 2 cents though!!<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000019||Haze_Performance||05-11-2001||01:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B>well i hate to say it but i rode in archies car to and i was not all that inpressed! he told me that motor was at 270hp and the northstar is 290! archie got a head start on the nortstart-the northstar guy wanted to do a dead stop race and archie did a rolling start - we all watched as the nortstar pulled about 3 car lengths ahead of the finale! now i am not sure of the weight of the finale because it is a body kit as apposed to the northstar! also the motor in archies car is not a taxi cab motor-it is a tpi motor out of a camaro or firebird! i know you can put alot of upgrades to archies motor to get more hp-i would like to take a ride in pauls v8 and see how fast a more hp fiero is! but riding in archies finale was alot like riding in my 87 iroc 305 auto! it just did not feel extremely fast to me! just my 2 cents though!!<BR>Rob</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In 1992 I bought a 1990 Iroc. (305-Auto) I had a few mods too.. Archie's car is faster in my book.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">      </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||2
Z||000020||Archie||05-11-2001||11:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B>-i would of hated to be archie then!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First off you, & your purple 4 banger, needn't worry about being mistaken for me. So you were one of the guys standing in line for a ride in my car. Gee, I didn't hear any complaints at that time. <P>Considering everything, I was quite pleased with the results of our little race on Saturday. Someone said that NStar was a 290 HP version and I never claimed more than 270HP. His was a "Stomp & Steer" automatic, I had to change gears by hand. I've never claimed to be the best drag race driver & I'm definitely not the fastest shifter. I have not drag raced but maybe 20 passes in the last 10 years. I made 2 errors though, Error #1 was the rolling start. I was in the left lane on a 2 lane highway, a bit concerned about possible on-coming traffic, I felt that the time to do a stop then correct start thing would have increased the likelihood of ME finding traffic in my lane. The problem with a rolling start with a stick car is that you got to push the clutch in and get the RPM up before you launch, when this run started I was in 1st with the clutch out rolling at maybe 10MPH. All he had to do was stomp & steer, I had to bring the RPM up then take off...... he jumped out to about 3 car lengths at the start. Then my 2nd error was a late shift out of 1st, My valves had been floating at 5300RPM all day long, yet I tried to run it out further to make up for my bad start. So by the time I got out of 1st, I was 4 lengths behind, I kept up with him until well beyond 100 MPH. I'm happy with that. A 290HP Automatic Fiero SHOULD out run a 270HP stick Fiero with 2 people in it. <P>Now If I had showed up with a 400 HP engine and kicked his butt, then people would say I was picking on him.<P>The nice thing about a SBC engine is that if you want to up the power a little all you have to do is add a cam or change the heads or put a bigger TB on it. You can't do much of that with the Nstar.<P>You know, It's like Ricky Nelson sang, You can't please everybody..... you got to please yourself.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000021||2xsess||05-11-2001||02:32 PM||||Another question, does the addition of the Fino kit add even more weight?<P>All in all it sounds like everyone had a blast.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 05-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||FieroLisa||05-11-2001||03:12 PM||||"His was a "Stomp & Steer" automatic, I had to change gears by hand. "<P>It is my understanding that a manual Fiero has the advantage over an automatic one, esp for someone that has lots of experience driving a stick...||||reg||1
Z||000023||fldevel||05-11-2001||03:18 PM||||this has inspired mw to wash my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ..great pics ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||05-11-2001||05:18 PM||||I just want to say that over the past few years I have rode in a few V-8 Fiero's. They were all SBC's. The Finale is not the "fastest V-8 Fiero" and Archie does not claim it is. If I remember correctly, The V-8 is a crate 350 with TPI. The race with the Northstar was a "reaction race". I was standing in front of Paul's 88 Formula when the "race" started. First, Archie tried to take off and the N* stopped to line up, then Archie hit the brakes and the N* took off. It was more hesitation/confusion that caused the race to start awkward. As for Archie pushing the RPM's and messing up the shift, I couldn't say. KissMySSFiero was riding in the car during the race so he and Archie would know better. The N* Fiero jumped ahead and stayed there. The Finale wasn't too far behind. From my point of view, If both cars were set on a drag strip it would be a much closer race. Any drag racer will tell you reaction time is 1/2 the race.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Archie||05-11-2001||07:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>I was in the car when they raced.  .....<BR>and i got to see it all from the passenger seat.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Aren't you glad you moved to Indiana now?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000026||SloPonti||05-11-2001||09:04 PM||||well i am sorry archie but truly i was not all that impresed with that cars performance! that is not to say that your setup is wrong or not right for someone else! i could still see a v8 in my car but for my own preference i would need more hp! but that is just me! the way i look at it is i would hate to sell v8 kits and then not have the fasted one around-but then again that is just me! and heh-leave the purple four banger out of this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> LOL||||reg||1
Z||000027||Archie||05-11-2001||10:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B> the way i look at it is i would hate to sell v8 kits and then not have the fasted one around-but then again that is just me!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> LOL</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Let me tell you just how wrong you are..... the guy selling the kits should never have the fasted one around or even the best looking one. That would be bad customer relations, it would send the message that seller HAS to be BETTER THAN everyone else who buys his product. My pride is seeing the biggest and the best in the hands of my customers.<P>Right now, I have 5 V-8 Fieros, now which one would have to be the fasted one around? They can't all be the fasted one.<P>Pay attention & you may learn something.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000028||Dave Gunsul||05-11-2001||11:00 PM||||I would think that the LM1 that Archie has in the Finale has more like 260 or less HP.<BR>You have to understand that this is the bottom of the barrell V8 crate that GM sells.<BR>It's also all iron!!<BR>The north* has 190 HP and is all alum.!!<BR>I ran over when they lined up and it looked <BR>damn close so I don't think anyone should be bragging about the star at all especially when you compare cost.<BR>I too have to wonder what any of you would have had to say if Archie had used Jack or Rich Warbers 450+ HP V8's and completely destroyed the star.<P>One thing i'm sure that we all can agree on though is that it was sure fun to watch!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000029||northstar87||05-13-2001||11:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> <BR>Considering everything, I was quite pleased with the results of our little race on Saturday. Someone said that NStar was a 290 HP version and I never claimed more than 270HP. His was a "Stomp & Steer" automatic, I had to change gears by hand. I've never claimed to be the best drag race driver & I'm definitely not the fastest shifter. I have not drag raced but maybe 20 passes in the last 10 years. I made 2 errors though, Error #1 was the rolling start. I was in the left lane on a 2 lane highway, a bit concerned about possible on-coming traffic, I felt that the time to do a stop then correct start thing would have increased the likelihood of ME finding traffic in my lane. The problem with a rolling start with a stick car is that you got to push the clutch in and get the RPM up before you launch, when this run started I was in 1st with the clutch out rolling at maybe 10MPH. All he had to do was stomp & steer, I had to bring the RPM up then take off...... he jumped out to about 3 car lengths at the start. Then my 2nd error was a late shift out of 1st, My valves had been floating at 5300RPM all day long, yet I tried to run it out further to make up for my bad start. So by the time I got out of 1st, I was 4 lengths behind, I kept up with him until well beyond 100 MPH. I'm happy with that. A 290HP Automatic Fiero SHOULD out run a 270HP stick Fiero with 2 people in it.<BR>The nice thing about a SBC engine is that if you want to up the power a little all you have to do is add a cam or change the heads or put a bigger TB on it. You can't do much of that with the Nstar.<BR>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> I think I counted about 10 or so(I lost count) excuses.  You lost.  It happens to everyone at some point. I have lost before, and I just accept it for what it is and keep going.  I have nothing against small blocks because they have ruled the land for almost 50 years.  (Except the HEMI, LONG LIVE THE HEMI!!!)  I just wanted to be different.  That is why I went with the technology of the Northstar.  I know that there aren't as many parts for the Northstar but you will start to see them. They already have heads, cams, superchargers, exhaust, computer equipment, and intakes.  Think about it, the small block has been around for almost 50 years and the Northstar about 9 years.  Wow, it sounds like I am making excuses now, it must be contagious.  <P>Chris Moore<BR>ASE Master Auto Tech <BR>Auto Instructor<BR>1986 GT Convertible Northstar<BR>1987 GT Northstar<BR>1988 GT T-TOP 3.4 5 speed<BR>1988 GT T-TOP Stock||||reg||1
Z||000030||Slammed Fiero||05-14-2001||06:46 PM||||Cadillac Hotrod Fabrications and a few other outfits like TAD (Tim allen Designs, no webpage yet) Are building quite a number of parts for the Northstar. While it's popularity isn't as strong as the SBC , lots of hotrodders are turing to it because it's different than the same old small block.<P>When I worked at GM in research marketing I had quite a few conversations about the N* with engineers , the motor is full of potential. It's tuned to give the best mix of performance and smooth power delivery (emphasis on luxury) , the tranny is programmed to be very docile , the car is a real import fighter when it comes to technology.  Just think if the motor was taken to the other end of the spectrum tuned to be more of a monster. When I worked there people talked about John Mosses personal STS that had the limiter upper to 7500rpm on an internally stock motor , free flow exhaust. A slew of external engine mods , car was running right on the 14 sec/13 sec barrier. Whats an STS weigh 4500-600lbs?? There are guys on the net that just play with the tranny and shift points in there STS caddies and get mid 14's on them<P>I will see if I can't dig up some links<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Archie||05-14-2001||11:44 PM||||Pretty cute Chris.<P>I'll bet it just tears you up that the Nstar that beat me was built by Design 1.<BR>I know it doesn't help that Design 1 has cured the Driveability problems you've been struggling with for 4 years. And won't share the cure with you.<BR>I'm sure it kills you when you realize that I'll never go to another racing opportunity underpowered or unprepared.<BR>I know that you're angry that you've been proven wrong on the issue of durability of the Getrag transmission with V-8 power.<BR>I know it's tough that you can't dictate your opinion to others here like you can in your classroom.<BR>I know you don't like it when we can disagree with you without getting hauled to the principals office.<BR>I'm sorry that you loose count when counting to 10.<BR>Do you realize how petty & childish your last post sounds? It could have been written by one of your High School students.<BR>Remember the things you've said in this post, before the end of the year, I'll bet we hear all of your excuses And someone will be referring you back to this post.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000032||FieroLisa||05-15-2001||12:06 AM||||Archie- I have no problems with your mechanical work or cars, but isn't what YOU said just as childish as you claimed Chris's statements to be... "Sorry you can't count to 10"<P>Chris doesn't need excuses for his work: he's proud of what he does and does a good job at it.||||reg||1
Z||000033||Slammed Fiero||05-15-2001||12:07 AM||||Chris has a day job as a teacher so I don't think it tears him up that the N* was built by Design one. As well I'm in line to get a N* done by Chris, He just picked up a motor to do a conversion for another gentleman. I doubt a guy that is winning just about every show in the country , and is due to be featured in Pontiac magazine (I was there for the photoshoot) is too upset about anything. If I had his cars , or the skill it requires to build a complete reliable package such as he has done I would be pretty happy. <P>He is also working closley with John Lingenfelter on the so called driveability problems<P>Mid 13's , 24mpg , and an engine smooth as silk do not qualify as a driveability problems. Mr Lingenfelter invited Chris to his shop to tune the car because he was so impressed with the converison. I don't think he does that too often do you??<P>If the car is mid 13's with driveability problems as you put it, Imagine in a few weeks when it's sorted out, espically by a guru like John Lingenfelter. I don't think there is a person who can ignore the skill that he has when it comes to engines. It rivals just about anyones.<P>As for the driveability problems , I know exactly what has caused the slow Progression. Chris is 23 yrs old , I remember seeing his award winning 87 GT at the Michigan show 4 years ago , he was 18-19 when he built his First N* car , how many 19 year olds do you know that can do that?? before that he built a 3800SC Fiero when he was 17-18. He just bought a house , he has 4 Fiero's. Money is a big issue when you have lots of bills and your 23 (paying for school mortgage ect)!!!. He drove the N* car for 3 or so years before it even came close to looking like it does now. I remember seeing it when it was a bright Blue POS with a great drivetrain. The paint was cracked , the car was a 2500 car at best with a amazing engine conversion. <P>I don't remember what I was doing at 18-19 yrs old but it wasn't performing the most difficult engine swap there is.<P>We need more people Like Chris Moore and less people who are narrow minded. Archie is just mad because he has no power to kick Chris off the Forum.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-15-2001).]||||reg||1
